class Solution {
  public int[] chainTurntableProofStrip(ListNode head, int k) {
    ListNode a=head; List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();
    {ListNode previous=null,node=a;while(node!=null){ListNode next=node.next;node.next=previous;previous=node;node=next;}for(node=previous;node!=null;node=node.next)out.add(node.val);}
    return out.stream().mapToInt(Integer::intValue).toArray();
  }
}

privateData.editorialMd:
The working idea

Reverse the links of the supplied acyclic linked list, then traverse the reversed list to produce its values. An empty head produces no values.

Return the entire derived sequence, preserving its order.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n); space O(n).

